A('')
A('## 5. What the map should say (best guess)')
A('')
A('1. Matter rows stay on the patterns. Add the column Z2 charge (n2 mod 2). The travelling protected object is the Z2-charged quantum: (1,1), (3,1), (2,1), (0,1). The singlet patterns travel on the same routing without a gauged charge and without a native pointer.')
A('2. One flux row: the Z2 flux pair of a carrier, equal to class 3. Classes 2 and 4 and classes 1 and 5 are marked as not objects of the working law; keeping them needs a declared Z6 link.')
A('3. New rows: the quantum carrying a flux pair; the plaquette flux between carriers (unprotected once the field step is on); the six walk sectors (lattice-scale tower under M3); the mirror cones.')
A('4. No candidate: generations two and three; travelling gauge bosons; a travelling Higgs.')
A('5. Spin: by the declared pointer. The native spinor exists on the four Z2-odd patterns only and coincides with their weak index.')
A('')
A('## Evidence')
A('')
